    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d753">

                <pb facs="0962" n="952" sameAs="frus:frus1947v07/pg952"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/3–1347: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stuart</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-03-21T14:00:00-05:00">March 21, 1947—2
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>334. Navy Dept has instructed CinCPacFlt<anchor n="26" xml:id="d753-f1"/> (UrTel
                    554 Mar 13, 3 p.m.) that for policy reasons it is necessary that initial
                    significant movement in withdrawal Marines comprise transport out of China and
                    that it can be publicized as such.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d753-f1" n="26" xml:id="d753-f1-content">
                <p>Commander in Chief of the Pacific Fleet (Adm. Louis E. Denfeld).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
